🌐 Network Addressing Concepts

Network addressing concepts describe how data is addressed and delivered between devices on a network.

For an AWS Cloud & DevOps fresher, you should understand Unicast, Broadcast, Multicast, Anycast, Loopback, and APIPA clearly because they connect with IP addressing, routing, DNS, and troubleshooting.

1. Unicast ⭐

Unicast means one-to-one communication.

One sender sends data to one specific destination.



When your computer sends an HTTP request to a specific web server, the communication is generally unicast.

Key Point

One sender → One receiver

Used in
Web communication
SSH
RDP
File transfer
Most normal client-server communication

2. Broadcast ⭐

Broadcast means one-to-all communication within a broadcast domain.

One device sends data, and all devices in the relevant Layer-2 broadcast domain receive it.



PC1 sends a broadcast → PC2, PC3, and PC4 receive it.

IPv4 Broadcast

The IPv4 limited broadcast address is:

255.255.255.255

IPv4 can also use subnet-directed broadcast addresses.

Important

Routers normally do not forward ordinary Layer-2 broadcasts between subnets.

Used in
Some local network discovery processes
DHCP initial discovery
Key Point

One sender → All relevant devices in the broadcast domain

3. Multicast ⭐

Multicast means one-to-many communication, but only to devices that have joined a particular multicast group


A device that is not a member of the multicast group does not normally receive that multicast traffic.

Example

Multicast can be useful for:

Streaming
Real-time distribution
Routing protocols
Group-based applications
IPv4 Multicast Range
224.0.0.0 – 239.255.255.255
Key Point

One sender → Selected group of receivers

4. Anycast Basics

Anycast means the same IP address is advertised from multiple locations, and network routing directs the client toward an appropriate/usually nearest available instance according to routing decision



Why Anycast is useful
Lower latency
High availability
Traffic distribution
Global services
Real-World Connection

Anycast is commonly used in DNS and globally distributed network services.

AWS Connection

AWS services such as Global Accelerator use Anycast IP addresses to route users toward AWS edge locations.

Key Point

One IP → Multiple possible locations

5. Loopback ⭐

A loopback address is used by a device to communicate with itself.

For IPv4, the loopback range is:

127.0.0.0/8

The most commonly used address is:

127.0.0.1

This is commonly called localhost.

Example
ping 127.0.0.1

This tests the local TCP/IP stack without sending traffic to another device.

IPv6

IPv6 loopback:

::1
Why useful?

Loopback is useful for:

Testing the local network stack
Running local applications
Development
Troubleshooting
Key Point

Loopback = Device communicating with itself

